WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.892
Keep duplicate detection and duplicate resolution as two separate phases.

00:00:04.892 --> 00:00:09.537
Detection asks: which rows might represent the same entity?

00:00:09.537 --> 00:00:14.887
It can use normalized keys, matching fields, or similarity evidence.

00:00:14.887 --> 00:00:20.662
Detection is often intentionally broad because we do not want to miss possible matches.

00:00:20.662 --> 00:00:26.250
Resolution asks a different question: what should we do with those candidate records?

00:00:26.827 --> 00:00:32.159
Possible responses include selecting a survivor, merging selected fields, quarantining a group,

00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:36.909
or sending the records for manual review.

00:00:36.909 --> 00:00:43.229
Resolution should usually be more conservative because it can change or consolidate data.

00:00:43.229 --> 00:00:45.909
This separation gives you flexibility.

00:00:45.909 --> 00:00:50.994
You can improve your detection logic without automatically changing records,

00:00:50.994 --> 00:00:56.332
and you can apply different resolution policies depending on the risk and the business context.
